From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grigory Evko <grigory@evko.io>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 19:28:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] c++: plugin events for instantiations, sizeof, names, using
 forms, members and reflections

A plugin that checks C++ source sees the semantic tree after the front end
folds it.  Some facts are not in that tree any more.  An explicit
instantiation directive leaves no node in the tree.  The front end folds a
sizeof or an alignof to a constant before PLUGIN_PRE_GENERICIZE, also in
the argument of a call.  It also folds a use of a constexpr or consteval
function or variable in a constant initializer, a static_assert, a template
argument or an unevaluated operand.  A using-declaration, a using-directive
and a namespace alias at namespace scope keep no tree with a location.  A
reflect-expression and a splice leave only the entity that they name.

Six new events give these facts to a plugin while the front end reads
them.  PLUGIN_EXPLICIT_INSTANTIATION gives the type or the declaration that
a directive instantiates, the location of the directive and the extern
flag.  PLUGIN_SIZEOF_OR_ALIGNOF gives the operand of a sizeof or an alignof
before the fold, with the location of the operator.  PLUGIN_NAME_USE gives
the declaration that the parser resolves a name to, with the location of
the name.  PLUGIN_USING_FORM gives the kind, the declaration, the target and
the location of a using-declaration, a using-directive, a namespace alias
and an alias declaration, at each scope.  PLUGIN_MEMBER_ACCESS gives the
member that a class member access with . or -> designates, the type of the
object and the location, also for a splice and at instantiation.
PLUGIN_REFLECTION gives the entity of a reflect-expression and of a splice,
with the kind and the location.

The output of the compiler does not change.  PLUGIN_NAME_USE and
PLUGIN_MEMBER_ACCESS occur at each name lookup and at each member access,
so they are direct events.  Through invoke_plugin_callbacks, an empty
callback of PLUGIN_NAME_USE costs about 75 instructions for each lookup:
the event fills a data struct, starts the timer of the plugins and walks
the list of callbacks.  The front end instead reads the callback of a
direct event from a slot in plugin.h, and calls it with the facts of the
event as arguments, with no data struct and no timer.  An empty callback
then costs about 6 instructions for each lookup.  When one callback reads
a direct event, the slot holds that callback and its user data.  When more
than one callback reads it, the slot holds a function of GCC that calls
each callback in the list of the event.  register_callback and
unregister_callback keep the slot in agreement with the list, so each
event keeps one list of callbacks.

The four other events put their data on the stack and go through
invoke_plugin_callbacks, which now returns before it starts the timer of
the plugins when an event has no callback.  do_namespace_alias and
finish_nonmember_using_decl now return the declaration that they make, for
the event of the parser.

gcc/ChangeLog:

	* plugin.def (PLUGIN_EXPLICIT_INSTANTIATION)
	(PLUGIN_SIZEOF_OR_ALIGNOF, PLUGIN_NAME_USE, PLUGIN_USING_FORM)
	(PLUGIN_MEMBER_ACCESS, PLUGIN_REFLECTION): New events.
	* plugin.cc (plugin_name_use_slot, plugin_member_access_slot): New.
	(direct_callback, name_use_fan_out, member_access_fan_out)
	(update_direct_slot, update_direct_slots): New.
	(register_callback): Handle the new events.  Update the slot of a
	direct event.
	(unregister_callback): Update the slot of a direct event.
	(invoke_plugin_callbacks_full): Handle the new events.  Return
	before timevar_push when the event has no callback.
	* plugin.h (plugin_name_use_func, plugin_member_access_func)
	(plugin_direct_slot): New.
	(plugin_name_use_slot, plugin_member_access_slot): Declare.
	* doc/plugins.texi (Plugin callbacks): Document the new events and
	the direct events.

gcc/cp/ChangeLog:

	* cp-tree.h (struct plugin_explicit_instantiation_data)
	(struct plugin_sizeof_or_alignof_data, enum plugin_using_form_kind)
	(struct plugin_using_form_data, enum plugin_reflection_kind)
	(struct plugin_reflection_data): New.
	* parser.cc (cp_parser_lookup_name): Call the callback of
	PLUGIN_NAME_USE through its slot.
	(cp_parser_unary_expression): Invoke PLUGIN_SIZEOF_OR_ALIGNOF, and
	PLUGIN_REFLECTION for a reflect-expression.
	(cp_parser_explicit_instantiation): Invoke
	PLUGIN_EXPLICIT_INSTANTIATION.
	(cp_parser_namespace_alias_definition, cp_parser_using_declaration)
	(cp_parser_alias_declaration, cp_parser_using_directive): Invoke
	PLUGIN_USING_FORM.
	(finish_using_decl): Return the USING_DECL of a using-declaration
	outside a class.
	* typeck.cc: Include plugin.h.
	(finish_class_member_access_expr): Call the callback of
	PLUGIN_MEMBER_ACCESS through its slot.
	* reflect.cc: Include plugin.h.
	(splice): Invoke PLUGIN_REFLECTION.
	* name-lookup.cc (do_namespace_alias): Return the alias, or
	NULL_TREE after an error.
	(finish_nonmember_using_decl): Return the USING_DECL, or NULL_TREE
	after an error.
	* name-lookup.h (do_namespace_alias, finish_nonmember_using_decl):
	Return tree.

