+   the user data that it gives to that function.  When one callback reads
+   the event, the slot holds that callback.  When more than one callback
+   reads the event, the slot holds a function of GCC that calls each
+   callback in the list of the event.  When no callback reads the event,
+   the function is null.  register_callback and unregister_callback keep
